+## Request 20: Foreign Currency Support (COMPLETED)
+
+### What was done
+- Added RATES constant to src/money.js:
+  - EUR: 1 (base currency)
+  - USD: 1.085 (units of USD per euro)
+  - GBP: 0.8425 (units of GBP per euro)
+- Added convert(cents, currency) to src/money.js:
+  - Converts euro cents to target currency cents
+  - Returns ok(converted_cents) or fail(UNKNOWN_CURRENCY)
+  - Handles EUR, USD, GBP with proper rounding
+  - EUR to EUR returns same amount unchanged
+  - Uses roundCents for banker's rounding (half to even)
+- Added formatMoney(cents, currency) to src/money.js:
+  - Formats amount in target currency for display
+  - EUR shows € symbol: €1,234.56
+  - USD shows $ symbol: $1,234.56
+  - GBP shows £ symbol: £1,234.56
+  - Includes thousands separators and 2 decimal places
+  - Handles negative amounts with leading minus sign
+- Added UNKNOWN_CURRENCY error code to src/errors.js
+- Created test/currency.test.js with 33 comprehensive test cases covering:
+  - RATES constant values
+  - convert EUR to EUR/USD/GBP
+  - convert with unknown currency
+  - convert zero amounts
+  - convert rounding examples
+  - convert large amounts
+  - formatMoney with € $ £ symbols
+  - formatMoney thousands separators
+  - formatMoney negative amounts
+  - formatMoney unknown currency
+  - formatMoney padding
+  - convert then formatMoney chain
+  - Consistent decimal formatting
+- All 279 tests passing (33 new currency + 21 CSV + 10 late fee + 15 VAT + 16 overdue + 184 existing)
+
+### Design
+- Exchange rates are fixed in the code (not variable)
+- EUR is the base currency (rate = 1)
+- Conversion maintains precision through banker's rounding
+- formatMoney formats amounts already in target currency (doesn't convert)
+- Currency symbols precede amounts (€100.00, $100.00, £100.00)
+- Consistent formatting with thousands separators
+
+### Exchange Rates (units per euro)
+- 1 EUR = 1 EUR
+- 1 EUR = 1.085 USD
+- 1 EUR = 0.8425 GBP
+
+### Usage Examples
+- convert(10000, 'USD') → 10850 cents USD (€100 = $108.50)
+- convert(10000, 'GBP') → 8425 cents GBP (€100 = £84.25)
+- formatMoney(10850, 'USD') → "$108.50"
+- formatMoney(8425, 'GBP') → "£84.25"
+
 ## Next Steps
 - Available for future invoice features (persistence, API endpoints, etc.)
